WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Hundreds of miles south

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.469
of Gaza, turmoil in the Red Sea

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.903
not seen in decades

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.805
as Iran backed Houthi forces

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.440
step up attacks on ships

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.275
that they claim have ties to Israel.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.211
This has led to a major disruption

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.746
in global shipping as companies

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.247
such as oil giant BP

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.348
reroute vessels

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.883
all the way around Africa

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.151
to avoid attacks.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.020
CNN's Natasha Bertrand and Richard Quest

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.487
joining us now.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:23.089
Natasha, remind us who the who these are

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.090
and how is the U.S.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.959
responding to these attacks?

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:26.326
Well, Jake,

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.994
the Houthis are basically one

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.562
side of a civil war

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.231
that has been raging in Yemen

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.832
for the better part of a decade now.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.167
They are a rebel group

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.201
that managed to seize

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.737
control of many parts of Yemen

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.239
beginning in 2014.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.407
They now control

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.742
a large part of northern Yemen,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.610
and they have been

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.245
fighting a separate war

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.946
against Saudi Arabia

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.748
over the last few years, a war

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.650
that has abated over the last year

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.851
because of a cease fire.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.720
But they are also backed by Iran,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.622
which of course, is Saudi Arabia's

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.223
arch nemesis in the region.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.691
So a lot of different powers

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.359
at play here.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.561
But what the US is doing at this point

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.464
to try to deter these ongoing missile

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.132
and drone attacks by the Houthis

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.466
on these

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.368
commercial vessels is to set up

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.470
an international coalition

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.272
of maritime forces

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.174
that will basically be bolstering

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.842
the security in the Red Sea

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.510
and when necessary,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.578
escorting a lot

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.013
of these commercial vessels

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.614
so that they can transit safely

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.016
through the southern Red Sea and up

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.051
towards the Suez Canal, where, of course,

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.753
so much of international trade

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.121
and commerce passes

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.522
through on a daily basis.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.156
Now, the U.S.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.624
is saying that they are not necessarily

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.193
going to escort these ships

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.227
on a regular basis,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.995
nor are the other countries in the area.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.630
It's really just

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.732
an attempt to show

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.167
that the international community,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.569
the international shipping

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.370
industry, that they are there

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.772
in case they need them,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.840
and also to try

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.541
to show the Houthis

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.709
that they are prepared to respond

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.477
if they

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.411
do these additional

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.412
attacks in the future.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.746
But of course,

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.448
that has not worked in the past.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.583
Over the last few weeks, the U.S.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.951
has responded to these missile

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.618
and drone attacks,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.686
shooting down

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.854
several of the missiles

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:02.489
the Houthis have fired.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.224
It has not deterred them today Jake.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.825
Richard, what does this mean

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:06.826
for global trade

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.761
if ships have to reroute themselves

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.430
all the way around Africa?

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.233
Oh, it means about ten days, 15

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.767
days, two weeks round day

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.003
are eight and a half thousand miles

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.304
to go from Singapore up

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.373
through the Suez Canal to Rotterdam,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.509
11,000 miles.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.343
Only 12

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.844
if you're going to go around the Cape.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.179
I spoke an hour ago

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.681
to the CEO of Hapag-Lloyd.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.216
One of his ships

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.051
had already been hit

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.087
by one of these drones.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.221
He said if it had been hit

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:35.955
somewhere else,

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.891
it would have been much worse

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.058
for the vessel.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.527
It's going to be very difficult

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.328
to protect these ships

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.430
because there are so many of them.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.233
You've got to shoot down all the drones

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.701
and it becomes a long,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.503
costly, expensive affair.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.640
And so that's the economic balance, Jake.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.776
Do you send these ships around

00:02:56.943 --> 00:03:00.213
which will create supply chain issues,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:00.947
likely

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.282
raise the prices

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.251
and increase inconvenience, or

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:08.121
do you take the risk of the Suez

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.155
Canal route,

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:09.822
which frankly

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.024
no one seems to be prepared

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.893
to do at the moment, at the second?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.761
I'm afraid to say

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.262
the Houthis have the upper hand.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.697
And Natasha, we know that the U.S.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.398
has responded

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:20.900
by launching strikes at weapons depots

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.503
in Syria and Iraq.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.804
Our Pentagon officials are discussing

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.506
a more substantial response

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.974
to deter these attacks

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.109
by the Houthis to begin with.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:30.410
Well, look,

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.578
the Pentagon will always tell you

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.112
that nothing is off the table

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.314
in terms of a response.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:34.981
However, the U.S.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.950
has been extremely reluctant to bomb

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.984
the Houthies directly

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.319
and their infrastructure

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.386
also because there are several

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.755
political sensitivities at play as well.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.991
As I mentioned earlier, Saudi Arabia

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.725
and the Houthis,

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.927
they reached a very fragile truce

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:48.861
just last year.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.762
And the U.S.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.598
played a very important role

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.265
in that truce.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.166
And so the US does not

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.300
necessarily want to see

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.268
a new conflict

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.070
reopened in Yemen

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.738
against the Houthis, as well as,

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.707
of course, many Arab nations.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.641
They don't necessarily

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.743
want to see these conflict, these

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.578
this conflict escalate either.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.247
And so the US does not necessarily

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.581
want to open a new front here.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.650
But many critics are pointing out

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.451
that there may need

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:11.718
to be

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.186
some additional kinetic action

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.621
in order to deter

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.855
their attacks in the future

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.123
because they're just not letting up

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.124
with ballistic missiles,

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.292
anti-ship missiles

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.361
and increasingly sophisticated equipment.

